# =====================================================================
#  SCRIBBLD — .gitignore
#
#  This repository is PUBLIC (GitHub Pages requires it on a free plan).
#  Git history is permanent: a secret committed once stays recoverable
#  even after you delete the file in a later commit. When in doubt,
#  exclude it — a missing file is a minor annoyance, a leaked key means
#  revoking a credential three apps share.
# =====================================================================

# ---------- Credentials and signing ----------------------------------
# The APNs Auth Key is TEAM-WIDE — the same key serves SCRIBBLD,
# Men's True Aide and Hey Hun. A leak means revoking it breaks push for
# all three at once.
Apple APN Key/
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile

# App Store Connect API keys, wherever they land
AuthKey_*.p8
**/private_keys/

# Firebase client config. It ships inside the IPA so it is not strictly
# secret, but it carries a live API key and App Check is NOT yet enforced
# (see CURRENT_STATUS.md §5e) — no reason to hand it to a scraper.
# Keep your local copy; the app will not build without it.
GoogleService-Info.plist
**/GoogleService-Info.plist

# Firebase Admin service accounts — never commit these.
*serviceAccount*.json
*service-account*.json
firebase-adminsdk*.json

# Signing/export configuration: environment-specific, not source.
ExportOptions.plist

# Environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------- Generated ------------------------------------------------
# project.yml is the source of truth; the .xcodeproj is regenerated by
# `xcodegen generate`. Committing it guarantees merge conflicts.
SCRIBBLD.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
!SCRIBBLD.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcshareddata/

# ---------- Build output ---------------------------------------------
build/
build-sim/
*.xcresult
DerivedData/
*.xcarchive
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM/

# Swift Package Manager
.build/
.swiftpm/
Package.resolved

# ---------- Firebase / Node ------------------------------------------
functions/node_modules/
node_modules/
.firebase/
firebase-debug.log
firestore-debug.log
database-debug.log
ui-debug.log
*.log

# ---------- Local tooling --------------------------------------------
# Claude Code workspace settings — local preferences, not app source.
.claude/

# ---------- Xcode user state -----------------------------------------
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint
*.xccheckout

# ---------- macOS ----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# ---------- Internal working notes -----------------------------------
# Excluded from the PUBLIC repo deliberately. These are session handoff
# notes, not app source, and publishing them would hand out:
#   - the App Store Connect API key id + issuer (half a credential pair;
#     the .p8 itself lives outside the repo, but no reason to publish the
#     other half)
#   - Juan's iPhone device UDID
#   - a precise, current list of the app's unpatched weaknesses —
#     App Check unenforced, client-authoritative moves, the Hangman word
#     being client-visible, the Ink Pro seat limit being bypassable.
# That last one is effectively an attack roadmap. Keep both local.
CURRENT_STATUS.md
APP_STORE_SUBMISSION.md
